# Shell scripts must reach macOS with LF endings. A CRLF shebang line makes the
# kernel look for an interpreter named "bash\r", and the error it prints --
# "bad interpreter: no such file or directory" -- names a path that plainly
# exists, which is a memorably unhelpful way to lose an afternoon.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.command   text eol=lf
